>   Can somebody please E-Mail me or post a list of things to wish?

a good weapon: blessed rustproof +3 mjollnir/excalibur/stormbringer/vorpal blade
/snickersnee

(see artifacts spoiler at bottom of my message...and you want to get 
an artifact of your alignment, or else you'll be "blasted by its power"
when you pick up or wield it, which will take maybe 10 hit points away
from you)

a quest artifact for some class other than your own. (note that neutrals
can only get neutral quest artifacts, lawfuls only lawfuls, etc etc).

If wish is from a wand get either:
 3 blessed scrolls of charging (so you can recharge the wand)
 or, if neutral and not a tourist, the Platinum Yendorian Express Card
  (perhaps my favorite artifact...allows you to charge items like wands,
  etc).  

one of the following two is always good.  If i already have decent
armor, then I go with the shield, otherwise the dragon scale mail. If
you have many wishes, go for them both, probably.

blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail    Best armor in game...9 armor points
before enchantment, extremely light, confers magic resistance.

blessed +3 shield of reflection    Also essential.  Reflects wand and
magic missile attacks, breath weapons, etc.  

perhaps blessed rustproof +3 gauntlets of power or blessed fireproof +3
speed boots or blessed bag of holding or blessed +3 helm of brilliance
or blessed amulet of lifesaving or blessed amulet of magical breathing...
these items are all good, but are relatively easy to come across.   

good luck, danno


From: pmr@daneel.rdt.monash.edu.au (Paul Richardson)

This list is not necessarily complete or correct, but it's a good basic
guide. Info comes from my understanding of the source. (Highly suspect :-)

The 'mundane' artifacts. Lawful and neutral much more variety than
chaotics. Note the changes to some of the types of weapon when wishing,
e.g. Stormbringer is now a 'runesword' not a broadsword or ninja-to.

A class of monster in the Special column indicates bonuses against those
monsters only. The two columns '+hit' and '+dam' are the same as those
used in the Wheaton College Spoilers. I *think* they mean + to hit and
+ to damage, but not sure.

Name            Type              Align   +hit    +dam    Special
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Excalibur       long sword        L       5       10      seek, search, defend
Stormbringer    runesword         C       5       2       drain level, defend
Mjollnir        war hammer        N       5       24      electrical damage
Cleaver         battle axe        N       3       6
Grimtooth       orcish dagger     C       2       6
Orcrist         elven broadsword  L       5       0       orcs
Sting           elven dagger      L       5       0       orcs, warning
Magicbane       athame            N       3       4       stuns opponent
Frost Brand     long sword        N       5       0       cold damage
Fire Brand      long sword        N       5       0       fire damage
Dragonbane      broadsword        N       5       0       dragons
Demonbane       long sword        L       5       0       demons
Werebane        silver saber      L       5       0       were-things
Grayswandir     silver saber      L       5       0       (silver damage also)
Giantslayer     long sword        N       5       0       giants
Ogresmasher     war hammer        N       5       0       ogres
Trollsbane      morning star      L       5       0       trolls
Vorpal Blade    long sword        N       5       1       beheads!
Snickersnee     katana            L       0       8
Sunsword        long sword        L       5       0       undead

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

